{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786972806,"nonce":"gcwa5q27kU76WJPGNBo05e6orcw=","message":"Landed in `134f59e`.\n\nThe door carries the ensō bleeding off two opposite corners at `--oto-wash`, referenced as a mask from `web/public/motifs/enso.svg` (the mono cut, verbatim) rather than inlined a second time. The form stays bare on the canvas — no plate.\n\nThe carve-out works as the ticket specified and for the reason it gave: both ink spans stretch to `inset-0` of the wrapper rather than to the size of the art, so `clearColumn`'s `50%` is the wrapper's middle, which is where the form is centred. 400 px cleared against a 320 px form is 40 px of air on each side at every viewport width, with no media query. §M.9 now carries the ❌ row that justifies it — `--oto-text-subtle` at 4.37:1 under a flat 6% wash — and `ink.test.ts` recomputes it, so the number that argues for the geometry is itself a gate.\n\nNothing animates.\n\n**One thing the ticket did not know about, found by opening the page.** `flex-1` has never done anything on this route: the shell mounts it inside a plain `h-full` div rather than a flex column, so the wrapper has always been 435 px of an 827 px viewport and the composition has always sat at the top of the screen. Nothing noticed while the canvas was empty. With ink on it, the `relative overflow-hidden` this ticket asks for cut the bleed off at a hard horizontal line two thirds up the page — a rectangle, which is the one thing a brush must never look like. `min-h-full` on the same wrapper fixes it, and the composition is now centred as well.\n\nAlso worth recording: `-z-10` on the ink is wrong here and looks right. Nothing in this tree opens a stacking context, so a negative z-index sends the wash behind the page background and out of sight entirely. The ink is written first and the logo and form carry `relative`; two positioned siblings at `z-index: auto` paint in DOM or